<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8826" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coctĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		coquo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>burned</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lateres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 14 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laterculus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 56, 57, § 193</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Curt. 5, 1, 25</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muri (Babylonis),</span>”
				<i>built of burned bricks</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 58</span></i>
			; cf. Curt. l. l., and <i><span class="en">Just. 1, 2,
				7</span></i> (cocto latere). —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coctĭlĭa</span></b> , ium,
				n. (sc. ligna), <i>very dry wood</i>,
				<i>that burns without smoke</i> (cf. acapnos),
			Treb. <i><span class="en">Claud. 14</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Dig. 32, 55, § 7</span></i>.</div>
